DESCRIPTION:Time Control: Game in 25 minutes w/ 5 second delay.\n\nRegistration: 8\;00 AM - 8:30 AM (can also late join)\n\nRound Times: 9:00 AM\, 10:00 AM\, 11:00 AM\, 12:30 PM and 1:30 PM\n\nComments: 8:30 AM MANDATORY MEETING\nFAIR PLAY POLICY:\nFair Play: (taken from the chess.com website)\n\nNo chess programs or engines (e.g. Chessmaster\, Fritz\, Komodo\, Houdini\, Stockfish\, Chessbase with any active UCI engine\, etc.) can be used to analyze positions in ongoing games at any time.  \nNo outside assistance OF ANY KIND is permitted.\nFixing game results by arranging games\, playing with multiple accounts\, or losing intentionally is also against the rules.\n\n**SANITATION POLICY**\nAll players are required to wash their hands or use sanitizer before each round. Masks are optional.\n \n**REFUND POLICY**\r\nA FULL refund will be given to any request at least ONE WEEK PRIOR to any Summit School of Chess program\, tournament\, camp\, event\, etc.\n\r\nIf less than one week's notice is given - it is at Summit School of Chess's discretion whether to issue a refund\, credit\, or another form of compensation.
